**FIVE SITES, ONE CLASS -- the invalid-DIRECTION interrupt accesses:**

| site | offset | direction that is invalid |
|---|---|---|
| IRQStatus | `+0x180` | **WRITE** to a read-only register |
| FIQStatus | `+0x280` | **WRITE** to a read-only register |
| IRQRawStatus | `+0x184` | **WRITE** to a read-only register |
| FIQRawStatus | `+0x284` | **WRITE** to a read-only register |
| ENABLE CLEAR | `+0x18c` | **READ** from a write-only register |

*** `+0x18c` CARRIES AN EXTRA OBLIGATION THE OTHER FOUR DO NOT: the decline must NOT expose the
currently assigned `d->irq_enable`. ***  A read of a write-only register that returns the live
enable mask leaks device state the guest is not entitled to read through that address.

## *** THE TRAP THIS ROUND MUST NOT FALL INTO, AND IT IS ALREADY NAMED ***

The row records that **K1 must be repointed at `+0x18c` in the same commit as the fix, or the round
reads its own success as a regression.** K1 currently asserts that a kill arm *dies*; once the fix
lands, it stops dying, and an unrepointed K1 goes red on a working repair.

