5766-7.3.6  DMA Channel n DAC Address--Offset 94h/B4h
5767-
5768-       The DMA channel n DAC Address register (n = 1 or 2) holds the upper 32 bits of the 64-bit PCI
5769-       address. If this register has a value of zero, the PCI address is in the low 4GB of PCI memory space
5770-       and DAC cycles are not performed on the PCI. If the value is nonzero, then DAC cycles are
5771-       performed.
--
5792-      Note: This register does not increment during a DMA transfer. This means that a transfer that crosses a
5793-                4GB boundary must be performed with two descriptors.
5794-
