C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-436-# construction, so nothing here would notice if a future change broke the
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-437-# combiner registration -- the rows would keep passing via the real
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:438:# instructions and the coverage would silently vanish. Only a #349/#352-style
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-439-# fold-fired marker closes that; it is recorded in OUTSTANDING_BUGS, and the
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-440-# historical pre-#354 sweep (4/12, the eight DISC rows red) is what establishes
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-441-# that these rows discriminate at all.
--
