C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-705-#
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-706-# Each fold gets a pair so neither row can be vacuous in either direction. The
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-707-# `fires` row demands the marker AND the verbosity echo AND the six transferred
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:708:# values: without the echo a session whose verbosity raise silently failed would
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-709-# report zero markers and look exactly like a dead fold, and without the values
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-710-# the row would prove a line was printed rather than that work was done. The
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-711-# `quiet` row asserts silence at default verbosity and must never be rewritten to
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-735-#  the `quiet` rows is visible in one measurement. On a build with ONLY
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-736-#  netbsd_copyin's arming disabled, `A fold copyin quiet` still reads **ok** --
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-737-#  it asserts an absence, and an absence is exactly what a dead fold produces --
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:738:#  while `A fold copyin cold` goes red because it asserts a DECLINE occurred
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:739:#  (install 1, fire 0, decline 1). Measured 5 of 8 on that build, red at exactly
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-740-#  the three copyin rows, with copyout's four green.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-741-#
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-742-#  The install count is what makes the diagnosis one-read: install 0 means the
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:743:#  matcher declined; install 1 with fire 0 and decline 1 means the fold was
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:744:#  reached and turned the operands down, and the decline text names the clause.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-745-#  Every arm also asserts the verbosity echo and that r0/r1 advanced by the full
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-746-#  six transfers -- the latter holds folded or not, so it proves the program ran
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-747-#  without presuming the fold, which is what stops the cold arm's zero from
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-751-#  #361 adds rows for the last two folds that had #358 markers but nothing
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-752-#  exercising them -- the scope debt #358 was criticised for. Two shapes, and
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-753-#  they are NOT interchangeable:
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:754:#    xchg  declines at the MATCHER (install 0), because #342's `a != b` term
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-755-#          rejects the shape before anything is installed.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:756:#    scanc declines at a GUARD (install 1, decline 1), like copyin/copyout, and
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:757:#          has TWO decline sites -- the second reachable only after the first
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-758-#          passes, since the table address is computed from the byte just loaded.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-759-#          Both are exercised, with distinct reason spellings so a row can say
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-760-#          which page missed.
--
