C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1091-    #  *** `tail_acc_x' PINS A HOST DEATH ON PURPOSE AND WILL GO RED BY SUCCEEDING. ***
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1099-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1100-    #    tail_acc_x            CERTAIN red -- wants exit1, and the fix removes the death.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1101-    #    tail_acc              CONDITIONAL -- it counts the DRAW message SUBSTRING and
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1102:    #                          wants 1.  A fix that LATCHES the text without REWORDING it
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1103-    #                          still prints the first occurrence, so the row stays GREEN.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1104-    #                          It reds only if the message is reworded.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1105-    #    hi_draw, hi_rd_draw   NEITHER red NOR safe.  Both want count(DRAW) == 0, so a
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1106-    #                          REWORD leaves them green because the string no longer
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1107-    #                          exists -- GREEN FOR THE WRONG REASON, i.e. VACUOUS BY
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1108:    #                          CONSTRUCTION.  A reword silently blinds them; it does not
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1109-    #                          fail them, and nothing would say so.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1110-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1111-    #  *** SO THE DESIGN CONSTRAINT IS: KEEP THE MESSAGE TEXT AND ADD `(once)'. ***  That
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1112:    #  costs ONE oracle re-pin (tail_acc_x).  Rewording costs two re-pins AND silently
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1113-    #  blinds two further rows -- which is the worse half and is invisible to any gate.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1114-    #  *** AND THE OBVIOUS RE-PIN IS A TRAP.  DO NOT RE-PIN `tail_acc_x' ONTO `"exit0"'. ***
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1115-    #  Adjudicated 2026-08-31 by the flagship seat, which traced the channel rather than the
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1117-    #  survives").  Trace what that oracle can see:
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1118-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1119-    #    a future one-token death reinstatement -- `exit(0)' at the default arm instead of
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1120:    #    `exit(1)' -- prints the announce once and then DIES.  `how' is then "exit0", so a
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1121-    #    re-pinned tail_acc_x reads GREEN; `tail_acc' still counts its one message, GREEN;
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1122-    #    and no other session reaches draw_primitive() at all.  TOTAL ESCAPE, 29/29.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1123-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1124-    #  So the re-pin would MINT, at the exact site being fixed, the exact blindness the queue
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1125:    #  row `exit0oracle' was filed to describe: EXIT STATUS CANNOT VARY between `declined and
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1126-    #  then quit' and `died with status 0'.  That is knowable at WRITING time from the CHANNEL
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1127-    #  check -- name the mutant a row kills and the observable that differs under it -- and it
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1128-    #  is why that check is run before the table, not after.
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1138-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1139-    #  Oracle-correction ordering applies -- re-pin FIRST, measure the committed build red,
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1140-    #  THEN edit.  Without this note the red reads as a regression in THIS device.
