C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1229-#  ---- block was never invoked at all -- 28 rows, three denominators and its own
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1230-#  ---- sentinel check evaporating while the gate reported one red row about a
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1231:#  ---- different probe.  Silent coverage loss, and it defeated the very sentence
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1232-#  ---- that justified the block (a committed detector no gate runs is a wrong
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1233-#  ---- record).  Both sibling blocks sit at depth 0; the block's own zero
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1234-#  ---- indentation was the tell that it had been written top-level and pasted
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1269-#  WHAT THIS PROTECTS.  That arm used to do `*color = random()' with its exit(1) commented out, so a failed
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1270-#  pixel GET handed the CALLER a random value and draw_primitive() wrote it to the destination in the same
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1271-#  loop iteration.  DE_MODE_LIN_B (0x1400) is one of the FIVE modes crmfbreg.h documents and extracts to
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1272:#  tlb_mode 5, so it was reachable with a DOCUMENTED mode.  Now declined, with a latched announce.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1273-#
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1274-#  The probe is BOTH the rung-3 WITNESS (7/8 red on the pre-fix build under the re-pinned oracle, preserved as
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1275-#  artifacts/sgirandompixel/witness_20260906/prefix_repinned_RED.out) and the DETECTOR (kill table in
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1276-#  artifacts/sgirandompixel/killtable/: five mutants, all killed, BASE 8/8 opening and closing).
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1277-#
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1278-#  `lin_b diag once' IS THE ROW THAT NEEDED THE MOST CARE and the reason the probe draws a 1x4 rectangle
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1279:#  rather than a single pixel: with one pixel an UNLATCHED announce also fires exactly once, the count channel
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1280:#  cannot vary, and M_NOLATCH escaped 8/8.  Height rather than width, because LIN_A addressing is
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1281-#  `ofs = x & 4095' -- y is ignored, so four rows rewrite one byte and the VALUE oracle survives.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1282-RANDLOG=$LOGDIR/sgi_re_randompixel.log
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1283-python3 sgi_re_randompixel_probe.py "$PMAX" gate > "$RANDLOG" 2>&1 || true
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1297-    #  in the same diff.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1298-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1299-    #  *** CORRECTED 2026-09-07 (#505 pass 2, the kimi substitute).  This used to say a name of 16 or
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1300:    #  more makes the pattern "UNSATISFIABLE, which is the same trap in its other, SILENT direction:
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1301:    #  the check stops testing anything and stays green."  THE SILENT PART IS FALSE. ***  `count'
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1302-    #  returns 0, `check' compares 0 against the wanted "1", and 0 != 1 FAILS -- loudly.  Measured
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1303:    #  over rendered rows at lengths 15/16/17.  An unsatisfiable pattern is silent only where a check
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1304-    #  wants ZERO, which no row check here does.  The dangerous direction is the ONE-SPACE form,
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1305-    #  which matched `lin_b diag once' from `lin_b diag' and is what this block was written for.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1306-    for v in "live" "devsig" "copy lin_a" "lin_b not src" "lin_b is fg" "lin_b alive" "lin_b diag" "lin_b diag once"; do
--
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1350-    #  CHARACTER of margin.  If a name must grow past 15, widen the probe's "%-16s" in the same diff.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1351-    #
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1352-    #  *** WHAT A TOO-LONG NAME ACTUALLY DOES: IT REDS, LOUDLY.  The sibling block above says it
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1353:    #  "silently stops testing anything while staying green", and an earlier draft of THIS block
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1354-    #  copied that sentence.  It is WRONG, and the pass-2 panel caught it. ***  `count' returns 0
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1355-    #  when the pattern matches nothing, `check' compares that 0 against a wanted "1", and 0 != 1
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1356-    #  FAILS.  Measured over rendered rows at lengths 15/16/17: 15 matches (ok), 16 and 17 match
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1357-    #  nothing (FAIL).  The UNSATISFIABLE direction of this trap is the SAFE one for a want-1 check;
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh:1358:    #  it is only silent where a check wants ZERO.  The genuinely dangerous direction remains the
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1359-    #  ONE-SPACE form, which matches a LONGER name's row as well and was measured on the sibling.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC\regress\gate_arm.sh-1360-    for v in "live" "devsig" "copy lin_a" "rgb chan" "rgb not corrupt" "rgb alive" "rgb samemode" "rgb depth64" "rgb tiled" "rgb tiled64"; do
