1734-         ROM Read
1735-
1736:         The SA-110 is stalled while the ROM is read. Each Dword may require one, two, or four ROM
1737-         reads, depending on the ROM width (latched at reset from the ma pins and readable in the SA-110
1738-         control register). The data is collected and packed into Dwords to be driven onto D[31:0]. When
--
1776-              and prefetch data is valid, then the read data is driven on D[31:0] and the SA-110 is not stalled. If
1777-              it does not match, or there is no valid PCI prefetch data, the SA-110 is stalled while the 21285
1778:              performs PCI memory read. It becomes unstalled when the read data is returned and driven to the
1779-              D[31:0]. During the wait time, PCI write data in the Inbound FIFO (if any) may be written to the
1780-              SDRAM or the ROM.
1781-
1782:              The 21285 may read more than one Dword (referred to as prefetching) from PCI depending on the
1783-              contents of the prefetchable PCI range register (see Section 7.3.23). The prefetch read data is put
1784-              into the Inbound FIFO. As each Dword is taken by the SA-110, PCI prefetch address latch is
1785-              incremented by one Dword. If the SA-110 performs a read to an address that does not match PCI
1786-              prefetch address latch, then all prefetched PCI read data is discarded. Also, if the SA-110 does not
1787:              perform any external bus read cycles for two cycles, the prefetched read data is discarded; the
1788-              two-cycle count is reinitialized each time some of the prefetched read data is consumed by the
1789-              SA-110.
