1802-3.1.13
1803-3.1.14  The SA-110 is stalled while PCI controller performs PCI I/O read. It becomes unstalled when the
1804:        read data is returned and driven to the D[31:0]. During the wait time, PCI write data in the
1805-3.1.15  Inbound FIFO (if any) can be written to the SDRAM and/or the ROM. No prefetching on PCI is
1806-3.1.16  done.
