1818-
1819-        The SA-110 is stalled while the 21285 performs the PCI configuration read. It becomes unstalled
1820:        when the read data is returned and driven to the D[31:0]. During the wait time, PCI write data in
1821-        the Inbound FIFO (if any) can be written to the SDRAM and the ROM.
1822-
1823-        Both type 0 and type 1 configuration cycles can be generated (see Table 3-5 and Section 5.1).
1824-
1825:        If the PCI configuration read ends in a master abort, the read data is replaced by FFFFFFFFh.
1826-        Typically, this situation occurs when initialization code running on the SA-110 is scanning PCI bus
1827-        to determine what devices are present.
--
1839-
