3877-     For Dword aligned and unaligned cases, the DMA channels may need to read more data from
3878-     SDRAM than is transferred to the PCI bus for each burst. Figure 6-3 shows an example of this
3879:     case. The PCI address is 100h and the SDRAM address is 208h. To write eight Dwords at PCI
3880-     addresses 100h through 11Ch (a cache line), the channel must read three blocks from SDRAM
3881-     200h through 22Ch.
