3883-              The Dword data from SDRAM 208h transfers to PCI 100h, and so on. The first two and last two
3884-              Dwords are discarded by the channel, but still consume SDRAM cycles. When the next burst of
3885:              data is moved, the SDRAM block starting at 220h is read again, and the first two Dwords are
3886-              discarded.
