1780-              SDRAM or the ROM.
1781-
1782:              The 21285 may read more than one Dword (referred to as prefetching) from PCI depending on the
1783-              contents of the prefetchable PCI range register (see Section 7.3.23). The prefetch read data is put
1784:              into the Inbound FIFO. As each Dword is taken by the SA-110, PCI prefetch address latch is
1785:              incremented by one Dword. If the SA-110 performs a read to an address that does not match PCI
1786-              prefetch address latch, then all prefetched PCI read data is discarded. Also, if the SA-110 does not
1787:              perform any external bus read cycles for two cycles, the prefetched read data is discarded; the
1788:              two-cycle count is reinitialized each time some of the prefetched read data is consumed by the
1789-              SA-110.
1790-
