1939-
1940-       The PCI memory write data is collected in the Inbound FIFO and written to SDRAM at a later
1941:       time. The 21285 requests the SDRAM at the end of each eight Dword boundary of the PCI burst
1942-       (or at the end of the burst).
1943-
1944-       If PCI address bits [1:0] are not 00 (that is, not linear increment mode), and the master attempts to
1945:       continue the burst past the first Dword, the 21285 signals a target disconnect.
1946-
