1985-              Subsequent SDRAM addresses in the burst are incremented by four.
1986-
1987:              The SDRAM dqm signals are asserted for each Dword according to the corresponding byte enable
1988-              from PCI. If the byte enable is not asserted, then the corresponding dqm signal is not asserted.
1989-
1990:              If fewer than five Dwords are available in the Inbound FIFO at the start of the write, the 21285
1991-              signals retry to the PCI master. If the Inbound FIFO fills during the write, the 21285 signals target
1992-              disconnect to the PCI master.
