2059-3.2.4         If the delayed read latch is full and a new read to a different address is attempted, that read gets a
2060:3.2.5         retry and no change is made in the delayed read latch. In other words, the new read does not
2061-              displace the in-progress read.
2062-
2063-              A memory read multiple command initiates streaming prefetch from SDRAM so that it can supply
2064:              read data at the maximum PCI bus data rate. Streaming prefetch works as follows:
2065-
2066:               � The 21285 reads 32 Dwords when the read is initially queued. This means that the address
2067-
2068:                   must be aligned to 32 Dwords.
2069-
2070-               � When the PCI master repeats the read, the 21285 starts to deliver data. When the PCI master
2071-
2072:                   consumes the 17th Dword, the 21285 reads the next 16 Dwords from SDRAM.
2073-
2074:               � As long as the PCI master continues to consume the 16th Dword of subsequent blocks, the
2075-
2076:                   21285 reads the next 16 Dwords.
2077-
2078-              The 21285 never stalls trdy_l while supplying SDRAM read data.
--
2080-              Streaming prefetch does not start if a PCI write to SDRAM or ROM is queued into the Inbound
2081-              FIFO between the delayed read being started and the read data being delivered. This allows the
2082:              write data to be written to SDRAM. In this case, only the first 32 Dwords are read.
2083-
