2440-              Read Bursting Policy
2441-
2442:              The 21285 attempts to read Dwords from the start address upwards, and continues to accept read
2443-              data until either the target disconnects or the 21285 deasserts frame_l. This situation occurs when
2444-              the 21285 has read all the data that it requires, or the Inbound FIFO becomes full. However, all
2445:              Dwords beyond the first Dword are optional. If the target disconnects after delivering the first
2446:              Dword, the 21285 does not resume the read at that time (for a DMA originated read, it resumes at
2447:              the address of the next unread Dword after the normal channel interburst delay). For an SA-110
2448:              read, all Dwords that have been read are eligible to be delivered to the SA-110 as prefetched read
2449:              data. For a DMA read, all Dwords that have been read are written to SDRAM.
2450-
