2847-
2848:       Memory reads and writes are done in bursts of four Dwords. For a read that requires less than four
2849:       Dwords (for example, a memory read from PCI), the 21285 discards the unused data. For a write
2850:       that requires less than four Dwords, the 21285 uses the dqm pins to inhibit writing to some
2851:       Dwords. The dqm pins also inhibit writing to unoccupied bytes. Table 4-1 lists the available array
2852-       sizes. The row/column multiplexer mode is the value programmed into the SDRAM address and
2853-       size register (see Section 7.3.13).
